All O(1) Data Structure
🟢 Problem Statement

Design a data structure that supports:

inc(String key) → Insert key with value 1 OR increment existing key by 1.

dec(String key) → Decrement key by 1. If value becomes 0 → remove key.

getMaxKey() → Return any key with maximum value

getMinKey() → Return any key with minimum value

⚡ All operations must be O(1) time complexity.
🟢 Example
Input:
inc("a")
inc("b")
inc("b")
inc("c")
inc("c")
inc("c")

getMaxKey() → "c"
getMinKey() → "a"

dec("c")
dec("c")

getMaxKey() → "b"
getMinKey() → "a"

🟢 Why Normal Map Won’t Work?

If we use:

HashMap<String, Integer>


To get max/min we must scan entire map → O(n) ❌

We need true O(1).

🟢 Core Idea

We use:

✅ HashMap → key → Node

✅ Doubly Linked List → ordered by frequency

✅ Each node contains:

frequency

set of keys with that frequency

🟢 Structure Visualization
Head <-> [freq=1] <-> [freq=2] <-> [freq=3] <-> Tail
          |             |              |
        {a}           {b}           {c}


Head → smallest frequency

Tail → largest frequency

🟢 Algorithm
🔹 inc(key)

If key new:

Add to frequency 1 node

Else:

Remove from current freq node

Move to next freq node

Remove empty nodes

🔹 dec(key)

Reduce frequency

If 0 → remove key

Remove empty nodes

🔹 getMaxKey()

Return any key from Tail.previous

🔹 getMinKey()

Return any key from Head.next

🟢 Java Implementation
import java.util.*;

class AllOne {

    class Node {
        int freq;
        Set<String> keys;
        Node prev, next;

        Node(int f) {
            freq = f;
            keys = new HashSet<>();
        }
    }

    private HashMap<String, Node> map;
    private Node head, tail;

    public AllOne() {
        map = new HashMap<>();
        head = new Node(0);
        tail = new Node(0);
        head.next = tail;
        tail.prev = head;
    }

    public void inc(String key) {

        if(!map.containsKey(key)) {

            if(head.next.freq == 1) {
                head.next.keys.add(key);
                map.put(key, head.next);
            } else {
                Node node = new Node(1);
                node.keys.add(key);
                insertAfter(head, node);
                map.put(key, node);
            }

        } else {
            Node curr = map.get(key);
            Node next = curr.next;

            if(next != tail && next.freq == curr.freq + 1) {
                next.keys.add(key);
            } else {
                Node newNode = new Node(curr.freq + 1);
                newNode.keys.add(key);
                insertAfter(curr, newNode);
                next = newNode;
            }

            curr.keys.remove(key);
            if(curr.keys.isEmpty())
                remove(curr);

            map.put(key, next);
        }
    }

    public void dec(String key) {

        if(!map.containsKey(key))
            return;

        Node curr = map.get(key);

        if(curr.freq == 1) {
            map.remove(key);
        } else {
            Node prev = curr.prev;

            if(prev != head && prev.freq == curr.freq - 1) {
                prev.keys.add(key);
            } else {
                Node newNode = new Node(curr.freq - 1);
                newNode.keys.add(key);
                insertAfter(prev, newNode);
                prev = newNode;
            }

            map.put(key, prev);
        }

        curr.keys.remove(key);
        if(curr.keys.isEmpty())
            remove(curr);
    }

    public String getMaxKey() {
        if(tail.prev == head)
            return "";
        return tail.prev.keys.iterator().next();
    }

    public String getMinKey() {
        if(head.next == tail)
            return "";
        return head.next.keys.iterator().next();
    }

    private void insertAfter(Node prev, Node node) {
        node.next = prev.next;
        node.prev = prev;
        prev.next.prev = node;
        prev.next = node;
    }

    private void remove(Node node) {
        node.prev.next = node.next;
        node.next.prev = node.prev;
    }
}

🟢 Line by Line Explanation (Important for Interviews)
✅ Node Class
class Node {
    int freq;
    Set<String> keys;
    Node prev, next;
}


Each node represents a frequency bucket.

✅ Constructor
head = new Node(0);
tail = new Node(0);


Dummy nodes simplify edge cases.

✅ inc(key)
Case 1: New Key

Insert into frequency 1 bucket.

If bucket exists → reuse
Else → create new bucket.

Case 2: Existing Key

Find current node

Move to freq + 1 bucket

Remove from old bucket

Delete empty bucket

✅ dec(key)

If freq = 1 → remove key

Else move to freq - 1

Cleanup empty nodes

✅ getMaxKey()
tail.prev.keys.iterator().next();


Last real node = maximum frequency

✅ getMinKey()
head.next.keys.iterator().next();


First real node = minimum frequency

🟢 Dry Run Example

Operations:

inc("a")
inc("b")
inc("b")
inc("c")
inc("c")
inc("c")


Structure:

[1:{a}] <-> [2:{b}] <-> [3:{c}]


Max → c
Min → a

After:

dec("c")
dec("c")


Structure:

[1:{a}] <-> [2:{b,c}]


Max → b or c
Min → a

